meta {
  name: Callback (OIDC)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/callback?code=REPLACE_WITH_CODE&state=REPLACE_WITH_STATE
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  code: REPLACE_WITH_CODE
  state: REPLACE_WITH_STATE
}

docs {
  Completes the OIDC authorization code exchange. This endpoint is called
  by the IdP after the user authenticates — it should not be called
  manually. It is documented here for completeness.

  Flow:
    1. Validate the state cookie (saidkick_state) against the state param
       — rejects with 400 on mismatch (CSRF guard).
    2. Exchange the authorization code + PKCE verifier for tokens at the
       IdP's token_endpoint.
    3. Verify the id_token signature + audience + expiry.
    4. JIT-provision the User row (upsert by org_id + external sub);
       update email, display_name, last_login_at on every login.
    5. Mint a short-lived HS256 session JWT and set it as the
       saidkick_session HttpOnly Secure cookie (TTL from AUTH_SESSION_TTL,
       default 8h).
    6. Clear the state cookie.
    7. 302 redirect to the `redirect` URL captured at login start.
    8. Write a `user.login` entry to audit_logs.

  Responses:
    302 Found     — redirect to the post-login destination
    400           — code or state missing, state cookie missing or expired,
                    state mismatch (CSRF)
    401           — id_token verification failed
    404           — organisation not found (org was deleted mid-flow)
    502           — token exchange failed or OIDC provider unreachable

  NOTE: This is a browser redirect endpoint. It requires the saidkick_state
  cookie set by GET /auth/login to be present in the request.
}
